  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Skies are clear this morning across\nnorthern and central Nevada. This is due to an upper level ridge\nover southern Utah. For today, look for mostly sunny skies across\nthe region with very warm afternoon temperatures. Readings will be\nin the 80s to low 90s. Some locales could see record to near\nrecord temperatures. Look for the dry conditions to continue to\nnight with lows in the 40s.\n\nA weak upper level trough will be approaching the region Monday.\nAt this time, there is limited moisture and instability associated\nwith this feature. Have added isolated showers and thunderstorms\nto portions of northeast Nevada tomorrow afternoon. Little to no\naccumulation is expected. Highs will be a few degrees cooler than\nSunday's readings with highs in the 80s. Lows will be in the 40s.\n\nUpper level ridging will build in again, dominating the weather\nfor northern and central Nevada from Tuesday through at least\nFriday. High temperatures will remain well above normal with\nreadings in the 70s and 80s with lows in the 40s. Winds will be\nlight each afternoon with occasional gusts to 20 mph.\n\nThe weekend is looking interesting though confidence is very low\nat this time. One scenario is depicting the remnants of a tropical\nsystem getting swept up in the flow with an upper trough in the\neastern Pacific. Current NBM forecast has increased PoPs and\nassociated weather elements for the upcoming weekend. No changes\nwere made to the NBM gridded forecast this far out and will need \nto continue to monitor the situation as the weekend draws near.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: Minor changes were made to the\nNBM forecast for tomorrow. This includes adjustments to the PoP\nand weather grids, adding isolated rain showers and thunderstorms. \nHigh confidence remains in the potential for near to record highs\nthrough Monday with high pressure. Confidence is still low for \nisolated showers and thunderstorms for far northern Nevada Monday \nnight into Tuesday as a weak upper trough moves into Nevada. There\nis high confidence in the return of upper ridging Wednesday \nthrough Friday next week. Confidence is very low with respect to\nthe upcoming weekend's active weather.",
